This file lists what Aether-Kit inherits from other work. Each entry names the
files that carry it.

AetherKit 0.0.x (https://github.com/bubstackdev/aether-kit, tag 0.0.7,
commit a013c45ec60d2292694a8e5f58ce31b228fd04df), Apache License 2.0, copyright
its contributors. These parts are re-expressed on Aether-Kit's contracts
(actor or lock ownership, AetherError, the 27 floor), not copied wholesale.
Their tests come over as specs, adapted to Aether-Kit's API:

- The cross-process GPU lease, in-process GPU admission and the fair queue
  (Sources/AetherHost/GPU/; tests in Tests/AetherHostTests/SharedGPULeaseTests,
  GPUAdmissionTests, FairInferenceQueueTests, with Tests/AetherGPULeaseHelper).
  The lease protocol (mkdir lease directory, pid file, rename-aside release,
  .reclaim flock and stale reclaim) is the one Atelier's SharedGPULock and the
  lab's with-gpu-lock.sh / gpu.sh use, kept wire-compatible. Atelier sources are
  copyright their respective contributors. FairInferenceQueue's design and its
  scheduling tests come from an earlier transport-independent admission draft
  for a host consumer.
- The model lifecycle policy (idle unload, memory-pressure release once per
  notice, the critical load gate and critical easing) and the memory-pressure
  monitor (Sources/AetherHost/Lifecycle/, Sources/AetherHost/ModelHost.swift;
  tests in Tests/AetherHostTests/ModelHostLifecycleTests).
- The model store's reader leases, per-installation advisory locks, abandoned
  stage recovery, free-space check, Hugging Face token scoping, redirect header
  policy, Range/Content-Range rules and the 416 restart, from LocalAssetStore,
  URLSessionTransport and ModelPreparation (Sources/AetherCore/Store/StoreLock,
  StoreLayout, and parts of Installer, ModelStore and HTTPTransport; tests in
  Tests/AetherCoreTests/StoreGapsTests).
- The background URLSession transport: task records, resume data, foreground
  redirect resolution and joining a running task after relaunch
  (Sources/AetherCore/Store/BackgroundTransport.swift; tests in
  Tests/AetherCoreTests/BackgroundTransportTests).
